Auto Ticket Classification Using Flow Designer
2.Requirement Analysis Phase
2.1 Functional Requirements
The system should be able to:

Detect when a new ticket is created.

Read relevant ticket information.

Identify the ticket category based on predefined conditions.

Set the appropriate category or classification.

Assign the ticket to the appropriate support group.

Set or update priority when required.

Add work notes or comments describing the classification.

Update the ticket automatically.

Handle tickets that do not match any predefined classification.

2.2 Non-Functional Requirements
The system should provide:

Reliability: The flow should execute consistently.

Maintainability: Classification rules should be easy to modify.

Scalability: The workflow should support increasing ticket volumes.

Performance: Tickets should be classified without unnecessary delays.

Security: Only authorized users should be able to modify the workflow and classification rules.

Usability: Administrators should be able to understand and maintain the flow.

2.3 Input Requirements
Typical ticket information may include:

Ticket number

Short description

Description

Category

Subcategory

Priority

Impact

Urgency

Caller/requester

Assignment group

2.4 Output Requirements
After processing, the system should produce:

Classified ticket category.

Appropriate assignment group.

Updated priority where applicable.

Classification-related work notes.

Successfully updated ticket record.
